---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import MediaPlaceholder from '../../components/MediaPlaceholder.astro';
---
<Layout title="Meet Sura">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container hero hero--split">
      <div>
        <h1>Meet Sura</h1>
        <p>Sura tends to notice the details. He is thoughtful, practical and more likely to consider what might happen next before rushing into a plan. But being careful does not mean he has every answer either.</p>
      </div>
      <MediaPlaceholder label="CHARACTER — full-body approved Sura" ratio="portrait" variant={2} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--surface">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What makes Sura, Sura?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>He likes to understand what is happening.</li>
        <li>He can be a steady counterbalance to Aya's energy.</li>
        <li>He is capable of being playful, not merely "the serious one."</li>
        <li>He can hesitate, overthink or make mistakes too.</li>
        <li>His relationship with Aya works because they bring different strengths into the same situation.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container hero hero--split">
      <img
        src="/images/characters/sura-aya-sandcastle.jpg"
        alt="Sura carefully building a tall sandcastle wall while Aya watches, delighted, nearby"
        class="sibling-scene"
        width="1400"
        height="788"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <div>
        <h2>Sura and Aya</h2>
        <p>Sura may try to slow things down while Aya tries to speed them up. Their stories work best when neither child is always right. They learn by dealing with the situation—and with each other.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .sibling-scene {
      width: 100%;
      aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
      object-fit: cover;
      object-position: center 70%;
      border-radius: var(--radius-card);
      background: var(--brand-soft);
    }
  </style>

  <section class="section section--soft">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Find Sura in</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Cards &amp; Games</h3>
          <p class="muted">Sura appears throughout the current Aya &amp; Sura flashcard decks.</p>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/cards/">Explore Cards &amp; Games</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Giving Thanks to Allah</h3>
          <p class="muted">Sura is part of the family story in our upcoming book, nearing completion.</p>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/books/giving-thanks-to-allah/">See the Book</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Adventure Club</h3>
          <p class="muted">Sura is one of the anchors of every monthly Club adventure.</p>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/adventure-club/">See the Adventure Club</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
